# OJ Packaging

Build the final Polygon package in a clean staging directory and use an allowlist. Do not zip the whole workspace. Exclude logs, reports, candidate pools, provenance, caches and temporary files unless the target package explicitly requires them.


## Golden FuraOJ / VNOJ template

Use the user-provided Polygon package as the structural golden template and conform to Fura Online Judge importer logic (`D:\Workspaces\Github\furavietnam\furaoj`, strictly READONLY). Default import limits & score: 1 GB RAM (`<memory-limit>1073741824</memory-limit>`), 1s time limit (`<time-limit>1000</time-limit>`), and 1đ problem score. Default language directories are `english` and `vietnamese`. Mirror `problem.xml`, `tests/`, `statements/`, `statement-sections/`, `files/`, `solutions/`, `stresses/`, `scripts/`, root scripts, `tags`, and checker/validator resource relationships as applicable.

Include the actual `files/testlib.h` used by the package when testlib is used. Testlib C++ sources must use `#include <testlib.h>`.

Do not invent or guess unsupported Polygon XML. Build a clean staging directory and verify all descriptor paths against actual files before ZIP creation.

After building the staging tree and final ZIP, run the offline-package-verifier in offline mode. ZIP readability alone is insufficient.
